---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/withBase';
---

<LegalLayout title="Customs & Liability">
  <h1>Customs &amp; liability</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">Summary of clauses 5, 12 and 19 of the <a href={withBase("terms")}>Terms and Conditions</a>. Last updated: 1 October 2026. If anything here conflicts with the Terms, the Terms prevail.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Khepia’s role</h2>
    <p>Khepia is a platform only. It is not a carrier, courier, freight forwarder, customs agent or postal service. It does not collect, handle, store, pack or deliver any Parcel. A Parcel is never in Khepia’s possession. Passengers are not employees or agents of Khepia.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Customs, immigration and airline rules</h2>
    <p>Each User is responsible for complying with the laws, customs rules and immigration rules of every country of departure, transit and arrival, and with airline rules (including baggage allowances and dangerous goods).</p>
    <p>Khepia gives no advice on the law of any country outside Pakistan and does not state that any item may lawfully be taken into or out of any country. Users must make their own enquiries.</p>
    <p>Only non-dutiable items may be sent. If any duty, tax, fine or charge is imposed on a Parcel, the Sender must pay it, and must repay the Passenger or Khepia any such amount they have paid.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If customs detains or confiscates a Parcel</h2>
    <p>The Passenger must tell the Sender and Khepia at once and provide a copy of any document received. Where a Parcel is confiscated because of its contents and the Passenger has complied with the Terms, the Passenger has no liability to the Sender for the Parcel, and the Deposit is returned under the Terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sender and Passenger duties (short)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sender:</strong> accurate declaration, weight and photos; non-dutiable, non-prohibited contents; pack and label correctly; accept that customs may inspect, detain or confiscate.</li>
      <li><strong>Passenger:</strong> inspect before accepting; refuse prohibited or mismatched contents; carry only in their own baggage; declare when required; deliver only to the named Receiver after CNIC match.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>The App is provided “as is” and “as available”. Khepia does not warrant Users, Receivers, Parcels or flights, and is not responsible for User or Receiver acts, Parcel contents or legality, loss/damage/delay/detention/confiscation of a Parcel, acts of customs or airlines, flight delays or cancellations, or inaccurate User information.</p>
    <p>Subject to what Pakistani law does not allow to be limited, Khepia’s total liability connected with a Booking is limited to the Commission received for that Booking. Claims not connected with a Booking are limited to Commission received from that User in the previous 12 months.</p>
    <p>Parcel Protection (if any) is not insurance and is paid only from the Passenger’s Deposit under the Terms — not from Khepia’s own funds as a general obligation.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Related pages</h2>
    <p><a href={withBase("prohibited-items")}>Prohibited items</a> · <a href={withBase("payments-refunds")}>Payments &amp; refunds</a> · <a href={withBase("terms")}>Full Terms</a></p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
